From fc5529f522a28df6ff5d5f7e572debc71d6f18e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xiyuan Xia <xiyuan@google.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 12:25:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [mac] Keep same clipboard sequence token for same changeCount

ClipboardMac::ClipboardChanged() is delivered via a posted task, so
there is always a window between the pasteboard reaching changeCount N
and ClipboardChanged() processing N. If a paste starts in that window,
Blink's GetSequenceNumber() mints token T1 for N; ClipboardChanged()
then runs and mints a second token T2 for the same N. Blink's
post-paste-event check sees T1 != T2, assumes the clipboard changed
mid-paste, and silently drops the insertion (beforeinput data=null).

This affects pastes of data copied outside of Chrome. It is hit reliably
by apps that write to NSPasteboard and immediately synthesize Cmd-V, but
a user who copies elsewhere and quickly pastes into Chrome, or pastes
while the browser main thread is busy, can hit it too.

Fix by only minting a new token in ClipboardChanged() if
GetSequenceNumber() has not already done so for the current changeCount.
Observer notification is unchanged.

Adds a regression test that exercises the real async notification path
and fails without this change.

Bug: 568453825
Change-Id: Ifa4ac6ce69c8c5b7422f0cbc5b525ff706180008
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8503629
Reviewed-by: Avi Drissman <avi@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Xiyuan Xia <xiyuan@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1712562}
